  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nThe Frost Advisory has ended this morning as rising temperature\nends chances for frost today. There could be some patchy frost \nthe next couple of nights, though coverage should be less than \nrecent nights and may not require additional advisories. \n\nModel ensembles indicate a closed low will persist off of the\nMid Atlantic Coast through mid to late week, with a trough \nacross the western CONUS. In between, a ridge is progged to\npersist from the Midwest to the Upper Ohio Valley/Great Lakes\nregion, resulting in dry and seasonable weather across the\narea. A weak trough is expected to cross the region on the NE \nperiphery of the ridge on Thursday, as the East Coast low exits \neastward. Little more than a few clouds are expected though with\ndry air in place. This will also likely keep temperatures near \nseasonable levels with some decrease in the 500mb heights. \nRiding should build eastward again by late week, with continued \ndry and seasonable weather.",
